{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAraMq8puWSkBYkVRHP7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The soft 404s come from `robots.txt`, and I've changed it to fix them. I haven't deployed anything or tested the new rules; I only edited the files.\n\n**Cause:** Each note page is a single HTML shell. `site/app.js` fetches the note from `/v1/notes/<slug>` and draws it. On 2026-09-07, `Disallow: /v1/` was added to `site/robots.txt`. Googlebot follows robots.txt for the fetches it makes while rendering a page, so it can't load the note data. `app.js` then shows \"NOT FOUND – No note lives at this address\", but the server still returns HTTP 200. Google reads that as a soft 404. Your browser and curl ignore robots.txt, so the pages look fine to you.\n\nThe Search Console files back this up:\n- **Rendered page:** the URL inspection of `drip-line-pressure` shows the NOT FOUND text and the generic title \"Field notes\", with HTTP 200.\n- **Timing:** notes last crawled in August (`first-frost-dates`, `mulch-depth-trial`) are still indexed. All four notes crawled in October are soft 404s.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`site/robots.txt`:** it still has `Disallow: /v1/`, plus `Allow: /v1/notes` for the public read routes the pages need. A longer `Disallow: /v1/notes/*/reactions` keeps the POST-only path blocked. `/v1/me`, `/v1/auth` and the rest stay blocked, because Google applies the longest matching rule.\n- **`site/app.js`:** the error screen now adds `<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"noindex\">`, so a future render failure won't be indexed as a page. The code now treats only a 404 from the API as \"not found\".\n\nThe cause and fix are written up in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Next steps:**\n- **Deploy and re-crawl:** deploy `robots.txt`, then use \"Validate fix\" in Search Console.\n- **Separate issue:** two notes (`bean-trellis-v2`, `greenhouse-vent-timer`) are \"Discovered – currently not indexed\". That is a slower problem with new pages, and it isn't caused by the robots.txt block. The homepage note list is drawn by JavaScript, so server-rendered links might help."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1471,"cache_read_input_tokens":24289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1471},"output_tokens":762,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bfc4501b-15e4-4fdf-b2cf-810625ab60a5","uuid":"2c894351-357e-4290-897b-d1a43c79455e","timestamp":"2026-10-19T03:05:26.589Z","request_id":"req_011CgAraMYXfqrkpB7uCKJoK"}
